{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/671443-2ed-jump-and-vigor-question","id":671443,"title":"[2ed] Jump and Vigor question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-19T16:18:42-07:00","id":671443,"title":"[2ed] Jump and Vigor question","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> Is happened to my PC's Coteries that they needed to flee through the roofs and now I have some questions about jump mechanich.<br /> Normally a PC can jump a foot for every success in Strength + Athletics roll vertically, and for a running jump he can travels Size + 4 feet per success rolled.<br /> Doesn't is it too variable? I means: Usually someone can jump more or less the same distance with up 2-3 feet of difference. With this mechanichs a PC with Strength 4 + Athletics 4 (that should be a great jumper) could jump sometimes 7 meters sometimes 2 meters... Is there an house rule to fix it or am I missing somethings?<br /> <br /> Second question is about vigor: it allows the PC to jumps successes rolled x (vigor+1) meters....without any distinction between vertical or horizontal or running jump. Is there something I didn't understand?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 09-19-2015, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T02:03:18-07:00","id":671731,"title":"","content":"Hi! I tried to tackle the whole jumping thing in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/41874-b-s-adding-physical-disciplines-help\">this thread</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T04:48:32-07:00","id":671817,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the segnalation. I read the post and I decided to fix the vigor jumps in this way:<br /> <br /> Vertical Jump: <br /> strength+athletics+stuff succes * (vigor+1) METERS<br /> <br /> Broad jump:<br /> strength+athletics+stuff succes * (vigor+1)*2 METERS<br /> <br /> Running Jump:<br /> size/3 + [strength+athletics+stuff succes * (vigor+1)*4 ] METERS<br /> <br /> So vigor enanches the jumps in two ways: instead of feet, meters (so a *3 basic modificator) and a *(vigor+1).<br /> Probably it could be a little excessive at hig vigor value but the description of the disciplines said that this is the reason behind the fly power of the vampire...so isn't unreasonable to jump 240 meters with vigor 5.<br /> what do you think?<br /> <br /> PS: anyway there is a really big disproportion between celerity and vigor; celerity 5 allow to reach at max a velocity of 216 km/h more or less....is not so exceptional in front of vigor effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 09-20-2015, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T04:56:50-07:00","id":671819,"title":"","content":"That's how I've always read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T06:50:46-07:00","id":671860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/671443-2ed-jump-and-vigor-question?p=671817#post671817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vertical Jump:<br /> strength+athletics+stuff succes * (vigor+1) METERS<br /> <br /> Broad jump:<br /> strength+athletics+stuff succes * (vigor+1)*2 METERS<br /> <br /> Running Jump:<br /> size/3 + [strength+athletics+stuff succes * (vigor+1)*4 ] METERS<br /> <br /> So vigor enanches the jumps in two ways: instead of feet, meters (so a *3 basic modificator) and a *(vigor+1).<br /> Probably it could be a little excessive at hig vigor value but the description of the disciplines said that this is the reason behind the fly power of the vampire...so isn't unreasonable to jump 240 meters with vigor 5.<br /> what do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I think that to make a running jump 240 m long with Vigor 5 and your house rule you need good stats and either Protean 2 or a lot of blood and/or luck since you usually get a success every three dice rolled on average.<br /> <br /> I also think that jumping is now super variable: Let's say a character, C, has Size 5, Str 3, Ath 4, Vigor 4, and basketball shoes. C rolls 12 dice.<br /> On average, C's running jumps will be 12/3=4 so [4*(4+1)*4]+2= 82 meters long.<br /> If C's a little bit lucky and gets 2 more successes (not that unlikely!) he'll jump 6*5*4+2= 122 meters.<br /> If C is a little bit unlucky and only rolls 2 successes he'll jump &quot;only&quot; 42 meters.<br /> <br /> It feels a bit weird.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T08:03:00-07:00","id":671944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/671443-2ed-jump-and-vigor-question?p=671860#post671860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I think that to make a running jump 240 m long with Vigor 5 and your house rule you need good stats and either Protean 2 or a lot of blood and/or luck since you usually get a success every three dice rolled on average.<br /> <br /> I also think that jumping is now super variable: Let's say a character, C, has Size 5, Str 3, Ath 4, Vigor 4, and basketball shoes. C rolls 12 dice.<br /> On average, C's running jumps will be 12/3=4 so [4*(4+1)*4]+2= 82 meters long.<br /> If C's a little bit lucky and gets 2 more successes (not that unlikely!) he'll jump 6*5*4+2= 122 meters.<br /> If C is a little bit unlucky and only rolls 2 successes he'll jump &quot;only&quot; 42 meters.<br /> <br /> It feels a bit weird.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes the weirdness you described is the main question about this thread.<br /> Even without Vigor's special rules (so the normal nWoD rules for running jumps) with your stats if you get 4 successes you jump 6.4 meters. With 2 more successes you'd jump 9 meters with 2 less successes you'd jump 4 meters....I think 2 meters of difference is really weird for every jumper... Vigor improving jump with a multiplier, &quot;multiply this weirdness.<br /> <br /> I mean: an olympic athlete in his various jump's attempts in a competition, can travel distances that differs between each other in the order of a few cm, not meters.<br /> The only way I see to fix this, is that any characters have a fixed maximum distance he can reach with a jump (for example the one obtained from maximum successes in the roll divided by 3); If the distance between (for instance) two roofs is a meter less than his maximum travel distance, the roll just say if the jump fail (0 successes - for example the PC's could stumble or take bad the distance for the run-up) or if the jump is automatically successful. <br /> If the distance between the two roofs is close to the maximum that the PC's can jump, the rool requires a number of successes equal to 3 (a meter in feet) minus the number of feet above the (maximu distance in meters minus 1).<br /> <br /> Anyway with vigor's rules the difference is not in feet but in meters.<br /> <br /> What do you think about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T08:36:30-07:00","id":672017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/671443-2ed-jump-and-vigor-question?p=671944#post671944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for example the one obtained from maximum successes in the roll divided by 3</div> </div> </div> </div>Infinity/3 is still infinity. Exploding tens, remember?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T08:45:16-07:00","id":672034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/671443-2ed-jump-and-vigor-question?p=672017#post672017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infinity/3 is still infinity. Exploding tens, remember?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I didn't say but obviously I meant like a killing strike: every dice is a success without ten's again.<br /> Strenght4+athletic4=8 successes /3 =3 (approximated in excess maybe to consider the tens rule).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T08:49:51-07:00","id":672036,"title":"","content":"Ah, yeah, that sounds a bit more functional.<br /> <br /> <i>Although...</i> it occurs to me that a professional long jumper is someone who has practised long jumping over and over again for several years. In other words, if I were to model them with the world of darkness system, I would feel comfortable giving them the rote action quality on running jumps. That would likely improve their consistency.<br /> <br /> If I were to attempt the same action myself, I wouldn't expect nearly as much consistency. Varying by a few feet? That's me on a <i>good </i>day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}